---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Pages from '@/components/motion/scenes/Pages.astro';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="page-transitions"
  title="Motion: change pages"
  description="The page slides forward or back with the direction of navigation: through navigate() inside a View Transition, or through Astro's client router."
>
  <MotionStage scene="pages" label="Live example: Change pages" height="sm">
    <Pages size="page" />
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    A page transition is a navigation, not a verb. <code>navigate(update, &#123; direction &#125;)</code>, exported from
    <code>@udixio/motion/page</code>, changes the page inside a native View Transition. <code>update</code> makes the change,
    and may be asynchronous. <code>direction</code> is where the page goes: <code>forward</code> (the default) or
    <code>back</code>.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import { navigate } from '@udixio/motion/page';

await navigate(() => showPage('roadmap'), { direction: 'forward' });
await navigate(() => showPage('home'), { direction: 'back' });`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The page entry is not in the main entry: a site that never changes its page does not load it. The route rules of
    <code>motion.css</code>, which the document imports, slide the old view out and the new one in, both fading, over the
    slow spatial spring. The direction is also set as <code>data-motion-direction</code> on the <code>html</code> element,
    and the transition's type is <code>udx-forward</code> or <code>udx-back</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Astro's client router</h2>
  <p>
    For Astro's <code>ClientRouter</code>, call <code>connectAstroTransitions()</code>, from <code>@udixio/motion/astro</code>,
    once in the layout. It gives each navigation of the router the direction that Astro reports, and starts no transition of
    its own: the router's transition runs with the route rules. It returns a function that disconnects it. This
    documentation site does this in its layout, and the forward and back links of the hero rely on it.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`// In the layout of the site
import { connectAstroTransitions } from '@udixio/motion/astro';

connectAstroTransitions();`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    A router is changed in the same way from any framework: the change of route is the <code>update</code>, and the
    direction is given by the link or the button that asks for it. Each example wraps the router's own navigation, as the
    code shows; the examples are not run, because each router is the application's own.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-pages" live={false} />

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions
    rows={[
      { name: 'update', values: 'a function, or an async one', description: 'The change of page. It runs inside the transition, and navigate() resolves once it is applied.' },
      { name: 'direction', values: 'forward · back · none', default: 'forward', description: 'Where the page goes: the new page comes from the right for forward, from the left for back. none keeps the browser cross-fade.' },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>The page moves on the slow spatial spring, and fades over the same time.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.slow.spatial']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>
    Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, <code>navigate()</code> runs the update alone, and
    <code>connectAstroTransitions()</code> does nothing: the page changes without sliding.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>navigate()</code> needs the View Transitions API: where it is missing, the update runs alone.</li>
    <li><code>connectAstroTransitions()</code> starts no transition; it sets the direction only.</li>
    <li>The morph of a shared element does not use the View Transitions API (see <a href="/motion/shared-elements">Morph one into another</a>).</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
